he API guarantees that each article's slug is **unique** (explicitly stated in the navigation map: \"prisma/schema.prisma — data model (Article.slug is unique)\"), and slugs serve as stable identifiers for article lookup, update, and deletion operations.\n\n## 2. Relationship Reflection in Responses\n\nArticle and profile responses include `favorited` and `following` boolean fields that reflect the **requesting user's** relationship to the content; for anonymous/unauthenticated requests, these fields default to `false` (as shown in the profile test: \"should get profile without auth\" expects `following: false`).\n\n## 3. Authentication Mechanism\n\nA request is authenticated by including an `Authorization: Token <token>` header (format shown throughout tests); when the token is missing or invalid, the API returns **401 (Unauthorized)** status (consistently enforced across all protected endpoints in the test suite).","ttft_ms":23016,"type":"result","duration_ms":26747,"uuid":"11f661f1-9183-4907-98a1-e191673020c6","ttft_stream_ms":2009,"time_to_request_ms":36,"first_content_frame_ms":2956,"queued_turn_count":0}
